<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.jambi.retirement-scan — the nightly cycle: property scan, email digest,
  and the finance export pickup (anything dropped in var/inbox, plus the IMAP
  mailbox when that route is switched on).

  07:15 local, once a day. RunAtLoad is false on purpose: installing the agent
  should not fire an API-spending run, and a deploy kickstarts the WEB job, not
  this one.

  On the schedule and the API budget: one idealista call returns at most 50
  listings, and the three configured areas cost 3-6 calls per run. Daily is
  ~120-180 calls a month, which is over a 100/month free allowance. Either
  keep this daily and confirm your approved quota is higher, or switch to
  Monday/Thursday by replacing StartCalendarInterval's dict with an array of
  two dicts carrying Weekday 1 and 4. The client-side guard in
  RETIREMENT_IDEALISTA_MONTHLY_QUOTA stops the run either way rather than
  letting the month end in 429s.

  StartCalendarInterval fires on wake if the machine was asleep at the
  scheduled time, so a sleeping mini catches up rather than skipping the day.

  The gui/<uid> domain is load-bearing here, not just convenient. Listing
  assessment and the board summary run through the Antigravity CLI on its
  Gemini subscription, and that credential lives in the console user's login
  Keychain -- which an ssh session cannot read. Bootstrapped into gui/<uid>
  this job runs inside that session and can. Run the same command over plain
  ssh and the CLI comes back logged out, the assessment returns nothing, and
  every listing scores on numeric signals alone. `./retire doctor` reports
  which backend is actually in use, and says so when it is not the one
  ASK_DEFAULT_PROVIDER asks for.

  SHELL. /bin/zsh -lc, not bash. This is a zsh account: a login bash reads
  ~/.bash_profile and never touches ~/.zshrc or ~/.zprofile, so `bash -lc` here
  produced a bare PATH and every AI backend reported itself missing on a machine
  where all of them work from a Terminal. trading-helper hit the same wall and
  worked around it by hardcoding absolute paths (see tools/watchdog.py's
  CLOUDFLARED_PATHS); this uses the right shell AND pins absolute paths in .env,
  because either alone is one machine change away from breaking again.

  Install: scripts/install_agents.sh
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.jambi.retirement-scan</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/zsh</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <string>cd /Users/jambimac/repo/retirement &amp;&amp; ./retire cycle</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>15</integer>
  </dict>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
  <key>AbandonProcessGroup</key>
  <true/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/jambimac/repo/retirement/logs/scan.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/jambimac/repo/retirement/logs/scan.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
